exit=0
--- stdout ---
Replace the configuration of the remote syslog sink the audit trail is
forwarded to (POST /audit/sink).

This REPLACES the configuration; it does not patch it. The endpoint takes a
whole sink, so every invocation sends one: a flag you leave out is sent as
its default, not kept from what the gateway had. To change one field, pass
the other fields again. Read the current configuration first with
'loxicmd get audit-sink'.

--address and --ca-bundle are required to configure a sink. The receiver's
certificate is always verified against the bundle and there is no mode that
disables verification, so there is no default the CLI could supply for it.
The bundle is a path on the GATEWAY's filesystem, not this host's, and the
gateway refuses a bundle it cannot read. --client-cert and --client-key are
for mutual TLS and must be given together or not at all.

--disable removes the sink: the gateway closes the session, forgets the
configuration, and the trail continues locally. Records already written stay
on disk; forwarding simply stops.

--facility takes 1-23. The gateway reads a facility of 0 as "not set" and
substitutes 13, so facility 0 (kernel) cannot be selected through this API;
the flag is documented as 1-23 rather than promising a value that does not
arrive.

If the outcome of the change cannot be confirmed (timeout, broken
connection), the command fails with reason 'recovery-required' and never
claims success - verify with 'loxicmd get audit-sink'.

ex)
	loxicmd set audit-sink --address siem.example.com:6514 --ca-bundle /etc/loxilb/siem-ca.pem
	loxicmd set audit-sink --address siem.example.com:6514 --ca-bundle /etc/loxilb/siem-ca.pem \
		--server-name siem.corp.example.com --facility 13 --max-frame-bytes 8192
	loxicmd set audit-sink --address siem.example.com:6514 --ca-bundle /etc/loxilb/siem-ca.pem \
		--client-cert /etc/loxilb/gw.pem --client-key /etc/loxilb/gw-key.pem
	loxicmd set audit-sink --disable

Usage:
  loxicmd set audit-sink [flags]

Flags:
      --address string        Receiver host:port (required unless --disable)
      --ca-bundle string      PEM bundle on the gateway verifying the receiver's certificate (required unless --disable)
      --client-cert string    Client certificate on the gateway for mutual TLS (with --client-key)
      --client-key string     Client key on the gateway for mutual TLS (with --client-cert)
      --disable               Remove the sink: close the session and stop forwarding (the local trail continues)
      --facility int          Syslog facility 1-23 (default 13, log audit; the gateway reads 0 as unset and uses 13) (default 13)
  -h, --help                  help for audit-sink
      --max-frame-bytes int   Largest message the receiver accepts; a record that does not fit is shortened at a field boundary and marked (0 = no limit)
      --server-name string    Name expected in the receiver's certificate (default: the host part of --address)

Global Flags:
  -s, --apiserver string    Set API server IP address (default "127.0.0.1")
      --bearer              Send the token as 'Authorization: Bearer <token>' (required by the inference gateway; disable for classic loxilb raw-token targets) (default true)
      --cacert string       CA certificate (PEM) to verify the server (https only)
      --cert string         Client certificate (PEM) for mutual TLS (https only)
  -k, --insecure            Skip TLS certificate verification (https only)
      --key string          Client private key (PEM) for mutual TLS (https only)
      --originator          Name this invocation in the gateway's audit trail as 'cli:<os user>@<host>', sent as the X-Loxilb-Originator header (for a service account driving the CLI)
  -o, --output string       Set output layer (ex.) wide, json)
  -p, --port int            Set API server port number (default 11111)
      --protocol string     Set API server http/https (default "http")
  -t, --timeout int16       Set timeout (default 10)
      --token string        Set Token for the API server (deprecated: the value is visible in shell history and process listings; use --token-file)
      --token-file string   Read the API server token from an owner-only (0600) regular file; replaces the deprecated --token
--- stderr ---
